From 4ec85ff188cde6424b508e79650b45967e88bdfb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: callan <callanf@nvidia.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 22:15:31 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 31/38] feat(retain): KvRetainCost (with
 kv_actions.retain_value.value: rebuild_cost): a session's value per block is
 the cost of losing its blocks over their number (class weight times min(1,
 rebuild time over the TTFT target) plus stall weight times the rebuild time,
 discounted by H / (H + wait)), so a long session is no longer the cheapest
 per block; with peers, a session another G2 tier also holds costs a KVCR
 fetch (RetainState tracks each session's holding tiers); without a cost model
 the value is unchanged; probe AISIM_VALUE_PROBE (one line per value-ranked
 eviction: sessions taken and the five cheapest kept, with value, blocks,
 weight, expected return); unit tests

---
